     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose is unsafe. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg per day. The maximum daily dose for immediate-release metformin is generally 2,550 mg, and many protocols cap it lower. A dose this high risks lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThe order may have been a transcription error, for example 850 mg or 500 mg three times daily, or 1700 mg once daily with the frequency mistyped. The prescribing clinician should confirm the intended dose and enter the order directly.\n\nAlso, medication orders normally need to come from a licensed prescriber, so I'd recommend routing this to the medicine team or the pharmacist on call. If a clinician confirms a corrected dose, I can enter it, with a note recording who approved it."
      }
